invariant: INV-43
file: p256.c
catches: p256_verify_equiv_test
reason: p256_ecdsa_verify hands the host verifier s where it takes r and r
  where it takes s. The DER reader and the device arm are untouched, so
  bin/unit and the 32-bit arm's proofs pass. bin/p256_verify_equiv_test
  holds the host arm to the device arm on every signature it tries.

--- old
    return p256_wide_verify_rs(pub, msg_hash, r_be, s_be);
--- new
    return p256_wide_verify_rs(pub, msg_hash, s_be, r_be);
